WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.022
Prior methods leave value on the table twice.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:07.779
First, most graph networks encode only atom
attributes and adjacency,

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:10.467
ignoring bond features and 3D geometry,

00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:15.982
even though shape and complementarity to the
receptor pocket make a good binder.

00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:19.498
Second, building molecules atom by atom gives long,

00:00:19.578 --> 00:00:23.221
unstable trajectories and hard-to-synthesize products.

00:00:23.301 --> 00:00:28.460
This motivates encoding spatial structure while
acting over whole fragments.
